- {"id": "F2", "severity": "high", "path": "scripts/watch_packet_1105.py:175", "evidence": "The packet checksum is read in one request and the content is updated in a separate request. If Eric or another process changes the packet between those requests, the update overwrites that change despite the stated outside-edit protection.", "fix": "Use an atomic conditional update against a revision or ETag if the available Drive interface supports it. Otherwise use a workflow that avoids replacing a concurrently editable file, and report the conflict rather than claiming the check prevents overwrites."}
- {"id": "F3", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/watch_packet_1105.py:242", "evidence": "If a pending success text fails again, the run continues. If a later rebuild also succeeds but its text fails, PENDING.write_text replaces the earlier unsent message. Eric never receives the first change notification. A pending message at the deadline is also abandoned when the job turns itself off.", "fix": "Keep a durable queue of unsent notifications, remove each only after successful delivery, and provide a durable recovery or alert path for messages still pending when the watcher stops."}
- {"id": "F4", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/watch_packet_1105.py:110", "evidence": "The Messages restart subprocesses are outside text()'s exception handler. If quit or open times out or cannot start, text() raises instead of returning false. On a success notification this bypasses creation of pending_text.txt; if it happens while fail() is sending an error, the error handler itself exits without recording or retrying the alert.", "fix": "Catch restart and retry subprocess failures inside text(), return a failure result, and retain the unsent notification for retry."}
- {"id": "F5", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/watch_packet_1105.py:301", "evidence": "A last check that fails at or after noon still executes turn_off() in finally. The source state remains unadvanced, but there is no next scheduled run to retry it. For example, a transient Drive outage at noon can leave the print packet stale even if service returns minutes later.", "fix": "Define and implement a bounded post-deadline retry or recovery path for a failed final check, with a clear failure notification and a way to retain the agent until that path completes."}
- {"id": "F6", "severity": "medium", "path": "scripts/watch_packet_1105.py:213", "evidence": "PACKET_BUILT is the Drive packet's creation time, not the time each source was downloaded for the original build. An edit made after a source was downloaded but before the packet was uploaded has modifiedTime before PACKET_BUILT, so seed() marks that newer source as already included and no rebuild occurs.", "fix": "Seed from the actual source fingerprints captured during the original build. If those are unavailable, conservatively mark uncertain sources as needing a rebuild rather than treating the packet upload time as proof of their contents."}

